{% from '_macros.j2' import section %}
{{ section(idx, finding, severity_label, repro_curl,
    suggested_title="Exposed config/dotfile served by " ~ finding.url.split('/')[2] ~ " — potential credential disclosure",
    impact=(
"A config or dotfile that is normally restricted to deploy hosts is being served by the web tier. "
"Depending on its contents this can leak: package-registry tokens (`.npmrc`), AWS / cloud credentials (`.env`), "
"Git repository internals (`.git/config`, `HEAD`), or session/CSRF secrets. "
"If the file contains live credentials, attacker-impact is **immediate** — publish-or-clone access to the org's "
"registries / repos / cloud accounts. Even an empty dotfile served by the application stack is a misconfigured "
"webroot that often exposes other adjacent files."
),
    validation=(
"1. **Confirm it is the real file**, not an SPA fallback. Many single-page apps return 200 with the "
"HTML shell for unmatched paths. Check the `Content-Type` and the first bytes of the body.\n"
"2. If the body is a config/dotfile, scan for actual secret material: `_authToken`, `aws_secret_access_key`, "
"`DB_PASSWORD`, `SECRET_KEY`, etc.\n"
"3. If secrets are present, **do not test them**. Report with the response excerpt only — using leaked creds "
"is out of scope on every major program."
),
    note=(
"False-positive risk on SPAs that return 200/HTML for arbitrary paths. The detection rule flags by URL pattern; "
"the evidence excerpt above must be inspected to confirm the response is the actual config file before submitting."
)
) }}
